# PART 1 — MISSION AND FINAL OBJECTIVE

You are continuing development of Wendoro UI.

Your responsibility is to transform the existing `@wendoro/ui` library into a comprehensive, modern, extensible, enterprise-grade design-system platform.

This is not a simple component-library redesign.

It must become the shared visual and interaction foundation for:

- All existing Wendoro products.
- Future Wendoro products.
- Independent SaaS applications.
- Multi-client agency platforms.
- Enterprise applications.
- Customer-facing portals.
- Internal business tools.
- Marketplaces.
- Professional service applications.
- Operations and administration systems.
- AI-powered applications.
- Other future business models and industries.

The system must support both small, simple interfaces and sophisticated enterprise applications.

The architecture must make future modules visually consistent, independently importable, maintainable and easy to extend.

The guiding principle is:

**Everything useful, one coherent design language, hybrid modular architecture, excellent experiences on every device, and no architectural dead ends.**

Do not limit the scope to an MVP or the components already listed in the existing README.

Do not introduce unnecessary complexity merely to increase component counts.

Prioritize working functionality, quality, reuse, consistency, performance and long-term maintainability.

